# procure-flow API requests
#
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and the JetBrains HTTP Client.
# JetBrains note: replace `{{create.response.body.$.data.id}}` with the ID from
# the create response (JetBrains uses response handler scripts instead).
#
# Interactive alternative: open http://localhost:8080/docs after `make run`.
# Scalar includes an in-browser request client backed by the same contract.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

# Authentication is disabled in development by default, so these requests work
# without credentials. When AUTH_ENABLED=true, run the login request below: the
# REST Client keeps the HttpOnly session cookie and sends it automatically.
# Bearer credentials still work; add this header to any /api/v1 request:
#   Authorization: Bearer <token>
# The local compose stack ships with `local-admin-token-0123456789`.
@token = local-admin-token-0123456789

### Liveness
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

### Readiness
GET {{baseUrl}}/readyz

### OpenAPI document
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi.yaml

### Metrics (Prometheus text format)
GET {{baseUrl}}/metrics

### Log in (sets the session cookie)
# Demo accounts come from `make seed` or the compose seed service. REST Client
# stores the cookie and reuses it for the requests below.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@procure.local",
  "password": "demo-password-123"
}

### Current session
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me

### Log out (clears the session cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout

### Create procurement
# @name create
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Laptop procurement for engineering",
  "description": "20 units of development laptops",
  "department": "Engineering",
  "requester": "Amir",
  "amount": 250000000,
  "currency": "IDR"
}

### Create procurement with an idempotency key
# Run this request twice: the second response is replayed from the first and
# carries `Idempotent-Replayed: true`, so no duplicate is created.
# @name createIdempotent
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-create-0001

{
  "title": "Idempotent laptop procurement",
  "description": "Retry-safe request",
  "department": "Engineering",
  "requester": "Amir",
  "amount": 15000000,
  "currency": "IDR"
}

### Error: idempotency key reused with a different body (422)
# Send after `createIdempotent`; the key is already bound to another payload.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-create-0001

{
  "title": "Different payload for the same key",
  "department": "Engineering",
  "amount": 1,
  "currency": "IDR"
}

### List procurements (defaults)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements

### List with filter and search
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements?status=submitted&q=laptop&page=1&page_size=10

### Get procurement by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements/{{create.response.body.$.data.id}}

### Audit trail (newest first, first page)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements/{{create.response.body.$.data.id}}/audit?page=1&page_size=20

### Submit procurement
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements/{{create.response.body.$.data.id}}/submit

### Approve procurement
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements/{{create.response.body.$.data.id}}/approve

### Reject procurement
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements/{{create.response.body.$.data.id}}/reject
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "reason": "budget exceeded"
}

### Cancel procurement
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements/{{create.response.body.$.data.id}}/cancel

### Error: validation (422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "",
  "department": "",
  "requester": "",
  "amount": 0,
  "currency": "ID"
}

### Error: invalid JSON (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{"title":

### Error: wrong content type (415)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements
Content-Type: text/plain

{"title": "Laptop procurement"}

### Error: not found (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements/prc_missing

### Error: invalid pagination (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements/{{create.response.body.$.data.id}}/audit?page=0

### Error: rate limited (429)
# Only returned once RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=true and the caller's bucket is empty.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements

### Error: method not allowed (405)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/procurements
